      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SAVVY HALLIE (1) tough on pace mare resuming. Won the G2 Light Fingers Stakes last February over the 1200m defeating APOCALYPTIC on the good surface. Is more effective on a rain affected track and she looks ready to go with the two trials. Will take catching. APOCALYPTIC (2) resumes. Flight Stakes winner in the spring and had mixed luck in the two runs over the summer months. Looks to have strengthened over the break and big things are expected this campaign after the two sharp trials. GATWICK (9) huge jump in class on the limit weight and can run a race here deep into the campaign. Speared across from the wide draw to lead throughout over 1200m at Rosehill in BM72 grade. Should get her preferred conditions and not to be underestimated. PRIMA BELLA (6) keeps raising the bar with the two wins in succession and stretches out to the 1100m for the first time today. Senior rider goes on and stays in the mix. STARDOM (8) speedy mare who returns with the two sound trials. Keep safe.",
